This project uses **Conventional Commits**:

```
<type>(<optional scope>): <subject>

<optional body — why, not what>
<optional footer — BREAKING CHANGE: …, refs #123>
```

Types: `feat` (new behaviour), `fix` (bug fix), `refactor` (no behaviour
change), `perf`, `test`, `docs`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `style` (formatting
only). The scope is the area touched (`auth`, `billing`, `orders`) and is
optional — omit it rather than inventing one.

- `feat` and `fix` describe user-visible change; everything else does not.
- A breaking change adds a `!` after the type (`feat!:`) **and** a
  `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer explaining the migration.
- Subject in the imperative, lower case after the colon, no trailing period.
